{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310628,"nonce":"cUtp8TO6gNQmZGjI0KR9vBIZaI4=","title":"Cross-context iface return-type erasure FIXED — late MIR re-resolve + W0014/W0015 diagnostics covers both property AND method dispatch","message":"**Status: FIXED end-to-end.**\n\nWhen an interface method (e.g. `Tokenizer.encode(s):Array\u003cInt\u003e`)\nis called and the implementation lives in a *different compilation\ncontext* (separate BLADE-cached file), TAST cannot resolve the\nreturn type and erases it to `Dynamic`. The actual call-site MIR\nvalue is still the raw runtime pointer; downstream consumers used\nto route through Dynamic-dispatch paths and crash (`.push()` →\nSIGSEGV) or misbehave (`==` → boxed equality).\n\n**The compiler-side fix** — late re-resolve at MIR lowering:\n\n1. **Iface dispatch site** (`hir_to_mir.rs:9388+` and `11930+`):\n   call `resolve_interface_method_return_type_full` which\n   string-compares method names against the cross-file\n   `interface_method_return_types` map. Raw InternedString ids\n   don't survive BLADE save/load — must compare via interner.\n   Accepts the entry whenever its TypeKind is more specific than\n   `Dynamic` — `Array\u003cInt\u003e` etc. all convert to `Ptr(Void)` at\n   IR level, so the filter must compare TypeKinds, NOT IrTypes.\n2. **Result tracking** — when re-resolve succeeds, store the\n   call result `IrId → TypeId` in `interface_call_result_types`.\n3. **Let propagation** — when an unannotated/Dynamic-typed `var`\n   binds an RHS register that's in the map, store the variable's\n   `SymbolId → TypeId` in `var_concrete_overrides`. Fires when\n   the user's type hint is `Dynamic`/`Placeholder`/`Unknown` —\n   real annotations pin the type at TAST and need no help.\n4. **Receiver lookup override** — `effective_receiver_type(\u0026args[0])`\n   in the Call method-dispatch path returns the override TypeId\n   when `args[0]` is a Variable in `var_concrete_overrides`, so\n   the receiver-type check sees `Array\u003cInt\u003e` (or whatever) and\n   routes through the normal stdlib path instead of Dynamic.\n\n**Diagnostics** (rust-analyzer-style hints):\n- **W0014** (Hint, light blue \"Advice:\"): \"interface method\n  `\u003cname\u003e()` return type recovered as `\u003cT\u003e` at MIR; annotating the\n  binding site makes the concrete type visible to earlier compiler\n  passes too.\" Fires when re-resolve succeeded — encourages\n  annotation but the code already works.\n- **W0015** (Warning): \"cannot resolve return type of interface\n  method `\u003cname\u003e()` across compilation contexts — value will flow\n  as `Dynamic` and downstream `.method()` / `==` may misdispatch\n  or crash; annotate the binding site to silence.\" Fires when\n  re-resolve *failed* (method not in `interface_method_return_types`).\n  Suppressed for Void-returning methods (no value to misdispatch).\n  Deduplicated by `(method, file, line, col)` so generic helpers\n  don't spam.\n\n**Why annotations no longer required**: late re-resolve makes\n`var ids = iface.encode(prompt)` work as-is — `ids` gets the right\neffective type through `var_concrete_overrides` and `ids.push(99)`\nroutes through `array_push` correctly. Explicit annotations are\nstill recommended (W0014 nudges) because they remove the MIR\nrecovery work and make the type visible to earlier passes\n(better diagnostics, formatting tools, etc.).\n\nRelated: [[bugs_cross_file_iface_array]],\n[[bugs_blade_property_orphan]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_iface_method_return_dynamic` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}